ences with paths on  one side and the enclosure on the other  side I know it's not quite as  experimental as the tiger trail but it's  definitely a very common set up in a lot  of zoo so it was a good time to kind of  practice this sort of enclosure setup as  well trying to hide the cliff of the  path and the moats as much as possible  which was something that I was a bit  concerned about I know I tried doing  this during games come for my tiger  temple enclosure as well but I really  didn't have enough time to make it work  in that case so I decided to take my  time here and try to make this  transition work a bit better it's also  nice practice to build a viewing  platform which I hadn't really tried yet  which I'll get into later in this video  and finally I figured I could build  something similar to what Rudy Ren Kamel  did shout out to Rudy who is making lots  of planets ooh content  and I really recommend checking out his  stuff you've probably already seen it  because it's it's really making the  rounds but if you haven't yet check it  out  he made a giant winter dome that was  basically what gave me the idea of maybe  trying something similar I watched his  first video and I skipped to the end of  it at some point and right to the point  where I skipped he said ooh I can feel  you skipping to the end of my video and  I've never been caught off guard on a  YouTube video as much as that so that  was really scary but that aside he puts  out really cool stuff so check him out  alien come down in the description as  well if I don't forget because I'm  really good at forgetting links in the  description so yeah that's my whole  thought process and how I ended up in  this place where I am building an  exhibit that doesn't make as much sense  but I still think it's worthwhile to  keep it and to put out this video I made  it in the end so yeah there you go  also the exterior was really fun to  build the whole class structure I think  was quite successful and I would  definitely love to bring back structures  like this maybe a bit more interesting  and a bit more focused on design instead  of just building a giant archway and  putting gloss in it but it was really  fun to try and mess with the pieces to  try and make this building it's not too  different from things that have tried in  planet coaster but it's been a good  practice to mess around with the glass  pieces the steel pieces and even the art  shapes that we have in game to try and  make something that's almost a little  bit Calatrava ish the tiny bit I'm not a  starchitect my Calatrava is and the zoo  is no major city governing board with  the financial and political power to  afford such starchitect err but you know  it's a similar kind of idea very glossy  modern structure with these exposed  structural elements and just a very  sleek overall look now the exhibit  itself is basically a new place for my  chrisley bears I didn't really explain  this beforehand but  the way that I went about playing the  franchise mode is I first spent a lot of  time just building a zoo focused on  gameplay elements trying to get used to  how to care for the animals how to best  set up habitats and things like that so  that before I went into making scenery  habitats I would already know you know  what the gameplay elements are like what  I need to keep in mind to try and make  them actually work so what I ended up  with was a zoo that worked really well  and made a lot of profits as you can see  in the bottom left corner although of  course this is a this is a non-profit  zoo all of the profits to end up back in  the zoo you know of course but no  basically I I did that so I ended up  with this really kind of ugly but  functional zoo so I wanted to make sure  that at least most of the animals that I  have in there already I can give a  better habitat than they have at the  moment so that's also why I figured I  might as well start off with the grizzly  bears and give them a better place at  this point I was installing some panels  on the glass roof on the Sun side just  to make sure that it weren't beginning  too hot in there it's still a giant  glass building in warm climates but this  should definitely help also brings in  some shade into the interior area on the  size of the bears that is the guests  will still be in the more sunny side but  hopefully that should at least help to  some degree making this a believably  cool building cool in the sense of  temperature of course and at this point  I figured might as well put some  decoration on this building because at  the moment it's a bit too contemporary  and blend so I decided to put a sort of  silhouettes of mountains on it to give  it kind of the idea of North American  landscape of course it still doesn't  really fit into the actual Asian  grassland habitats or environments of  the franchise mode but still I decided  it would be a cool way to spruce up the  exterior of the building a little bit  and then the rest of the scenery overall  is just going to be very simple I put a  giant wall of blah  underneath this section I really wasn't  sure for a while what I would do with  the ground floor whether I would put a  solid wall or something like that there  but I think it helps a lot to just keep  it completely open and you know of  course the building is not completely  open it's mostly closed but to keep the  view of the outside mostly open so a  building feels much larger more open and  less claustrophobic than it really is  and that's basically it  I'm not sure to what extent these trees  would be able to survive in the climate  of this franchise mode but I'm just  going for a bunch of spruces and all  kinds of taiga and tundra temperates  bushes and trees and of course a lot of  rock work you can't forget about the  rock work it's a common staple in zoos  it's a great way to hide again the  barrier on the outside and later on hide  some of the elements like cooling and  things like that